---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="NIST AI 600-1 & ISO 42001" activePage="nist">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <div class="mb-8">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-700 px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium mb-4">
        🇺🇸 US Framework
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">NIST AI 600-1 & ISO 42001</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-lg">NIST AI 600-1 (AI Risk Management Playbook) provides practical guidance for managing AI risks — here's what it covers and how it maps to ISO 42001.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- What is NIST AI 600-1 -->
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">What is NIST AI 600-1?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4"><strong>NIST AI 600-1: AI Risk Management Playbook</strong> is a companion document to the <strong>NIST AI Risk Management Framework (AI RMF 1.0)</strong>. Published by the U.S. National Institute of Standards and Technology, it provides practical, actionable guidance for organizations to manage AI risks.</p>
      
      <div class="bg-indigo-50 rounded-lg p-4 mb-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-indigo-900 text-sm mb-2">Key Facts</h3>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-2 text-sm text-indigo-800">
          <div><strong>Published:</strong> January 2024</div>
          <div><strong>Full Name:</strong> NIST AI 600-1: AI Risk Management Playbook</div>
          <div><strong>Parent Framework:</strong> NIST AI RMF 1.0 (January 2023)</div>
          <div><strong>Type:</strong> Voluntary guidance (not mandatory in US, but referenced globally)</div>
          <div><strong>Scope:</strong> Practical implementation guidance for AI RMF</div>
          <div><strong>Audience:</strong> Organizations developing, deploying, or using AI systems</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">While the AI RMF provides the "what," the Playbook provides the "how." It's organized around four core functions:</p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-4 text-center">
          <div class="text-3xl mb-2">🔍</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-blue-800">GOVERN</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-blue-600 mt-1">Establish AI risk management culture, policies, and processes</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-purple-50 border border-purple-200 rounded-xl p-4 text-center">
          <div class="text-3xl mb-2">🗺️</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-purple-800">MAP</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-purple-600 mt-1">Context, identify, and scope AI risks and impacts</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-xl p-4 text-center">
          <div class="text-3xl mb-2">⚙️</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-green-800">MEASURE</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-green-600 mt-1">Analyze, assess, and monitor AI risks</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-orange-50 border border-orange-200 rounded-xl p-4 text-center">
          <div class="text-3xl mb-2">🛡️</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-orange-800">MANAGE</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-orange-600 mt-1">Respond to, treat, and monitor AI risks</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- NIST AI RMF Core Categories -->
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">NIST AI 600-1 Key Guidance Areas</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">The Playbook provides detailed guidance across these areas:</p>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">1. AI Risk Management Governance</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Establish roles, responsibilities, accountability, and decision-making processes for AI risk. Define risk tolerance and integrate with enterprise risk management.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">2. AI System Context & Mapping</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Document AI system purpose, intended use, stakeholders, and potential impacts. Map benefits, costs, and risks across the AI lifecycle.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">3. AI Risk Measurement & Assessment</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Identify, quantify, and qualify AI risks. Use technical metrics (accuracy, fairness, robustness) and organizational metrics (financial, reputational).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">4. AI Risk Treatment & Management</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Prioritize and address AI risks. Implement safeguards, monitor effectiveness, and respond to AI incidents.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">5. AI System Accountability & Transparency</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Document AI decisions, maintain audit trails, ensure explainability, and communicate AI capabilities and limitations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">6. Third-Party AI Risk Management</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Assess and manage risks from externally developed AI systems, including vendor evaluation, contractual protections, and ongoing monitoring.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ISO 42001 Overlap -->
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">NIST AI 600-1 ↔ ISO 42001 Overlap</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">Both frameworks address AI risk management. ISO 42001 provides the management system structure; NIST 600-1 provides detailed practical guidance. Here's how they map:</p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
            <tr>
              <th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">NIST AI 600-1 Area</th>
              <th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">ISO 42001 Equivalent</th>
              <th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">Overlap</th>
              <th class="text-left p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">Notes</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">GOVERN: Risk management culture</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Clause 5 (Leadership) + A.2.1</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">High</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Both emphasize top management commitment and AI policy</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">GOVERN: Roles & accountability</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">A.3.1, A.3.2</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">High</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Direct match — governance structure and accountability</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">MAP: System context & purpose</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Clause 4 (Context) + A.5.2</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">High</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Context of organization + system requirements</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">MAP: Impact identification</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Clause 8.2 (AIIA)</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">High</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">AI system impact assessment maps to NIST impact mapping</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">MEASURE: Risk assessment</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Clause 6.1 + Clause 8.3</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">High</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Risk assessment + treatment process</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">MEASURE: Performance monitoring</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">A.8.3 + Clause 9.1</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">High</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">AI monitoring + measurement and evaluation</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">MEASURE: Fairness & bias</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">A.6.2 (Data Quality) + AIIA</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">Medium</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">NIST has detailed fairness metrics; ISO 42001 covers data quality and impact assessment</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">MANAGE: Risk treatment</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Clause 8.3 + Annex A controls</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">High</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Risk treatment + control implementation</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">MANAGE: Incident response</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">A.7.2 + Clause 10.1</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">High</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Incident reporting + corrective actions</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">Third-party AI management</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">A.9.1, A.9.2, A.9.3</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">High</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Third-party risk, agreements, and monitoring</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">Transparency & explainability</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">A.7.1, A.7.3, A.8.2</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">High</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">User info, public disclosure, human oversight</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-medium">Continual improvement</td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Clause 10.2</td>
              <td class="p-4"><span class="bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-medium">High</span></td>
              <td class="p-4 text-gray-600">Continual improvement of AI management system</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Key Differences -->
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Key Differences</h2>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-indigo-800 mb-3">NIST AI 600-1</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
            <li>• <strong>Voluntary</strong> guidance — not certifiable</li>
            <li>• <strong>Practical</strong> — detailed "how-to" implementation advice</li>
            <li>• <strong>Risk-focused</strong> — centered on risk measurement and treatment</li>
            <li>• <strong>US-centric</strong> — references US regulatory landscape</li>
            <li>• <strong>Flexible</strong> — adaptable to any organization size or sector</li>
            <li>• <strong>Detailed metrics</strong> — specific fairness, accuracy, robustness measures</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-blue-800 mb-3">ISO 42001</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
            <li>• <strong>Certifiable</strong> — can get third-party certification</li>
            <li>• <strong>Structured</strong> — management system with clauses and controls</li>
            <li>• <strong>Holistic</strong> — covers governance, operations, data, third parties</li>
            <li>• <strong>Global</strong> — recognized internationally</li>
            <li>• <strong>Integration-ready</strong> — works with ISO 27001, 9001, etc.</li>
            <li>• <strong>Audit-based</strong> — designed for external verification</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Practical Advice -->
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8">
      <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-green-900 mb-3">Best of Both Worlds</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-green-800">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span>✓</span> Use <strong>NIST 600-1</strong> for detailed risk measurement guidance</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span>✓</span> Use <strong>ISO 42001</strong> for the management system structure</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span>✓</span> NIST provides the "how"; ISO 42001 provides the "what"</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span>✓</span> Together they cover governance, operations, risk, and compliance</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span>✓</span> Many organizations implement both for comprehensive coverage</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-200 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-indigo-900 mb-3">Implementation Approach</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-indigo-800">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span>1.</span> <span>Implement ISO 42001 as the management system backbone</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span>2.</span> <span>Use NIST 600-1 guidance to enhance risk assessment depth</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span>3.</span> <span>Apply NIST fairness/bias metrics in AI system impact assessments</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span>4.</span> <span>Reference NIST 600-1 in documentation for US stakeholders</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span>5.</span> <span>Get ISO 42001 certified for international credibility</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Also mention NIST AI RMF -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Related NIST Documents</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-blue-300 mb-2">NIST AI RMF 1.0</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-300">The parent framework — defines the four core functions (Govern, Map, Measure, Manage). AI 600-1 provides the implementation playbook for this.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-blue-300 mb-2">NIST AI RMF Playbook</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-300">AI 600-1 itself — practical, actionable guidance with specific recommendations for each AI RMF function.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-blue-300 mb-2">NIST SP 800-218A</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-300">Secure Software Development practices that complement AI security requirements in ISO 42001.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>